# Complete Social Profile Data Pipeline — Apify → MongoDB → Bento UI

Redesign the data normalization layer so that **100% of useful data returned by Apify scrapers** is persisted into MongoDB and made available to the frontend. Currently, scraper services extract only a subset of available fields, and the `extractNormalizedRecentContent` function in `socialProfileService.js` discards additional metadata.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **No new API endpoints or services** will be created. All changes are within the existing architecture:
> - `server/services/*Service.js` — Expand field extraction from Apify raw data
> - `server/services/socialProfileService.js` — Expand normalization to persist all extracted fields
> - `server/models/SocialProfile.js` — Expand `recentContentSchema` with new optional fields
> - Frontend widget components — Already resilient via `extractRecentPosts()` helper; no changes needed

> [!WARNING]
> **Existing MongoDB documents will NOT be automatically updated.** After deploying these changes, each social profile must be either force-refreshed (edit the block's handle and save) or will update naturally when the 24-hour TTL cache expires. No data migration script is needed — old documents remain valid since all new fields have defaults.

## Open Questions

