### 7. Social Profile Service — Exhaustive Normalization

#### [MODIFY] [socialProfileService.js](file:///d:/MERN2/Hi-Profile-main/server/services/socialProfileService.js)

This is the **most critical change**. Overhaul `extractNormalizedRecentContent` to persist every field now being extracted by the expanded scrapers:

**Instagram normalization**:
```js
return posts.map(p => ({
    id: String(p.id || ''),
    caption: p.caption || '',
    imageUrl: p.imageUrl || p.displayUrl || p.thumbnailUrl || '',
    contentUrl: p.postUrl || p.url || '',
    likesCount: Number(p.likesCount || 0),
    commentsCount: Number(p.commentsCount || 0),
    shortCode: p.shortCode || p.shortcode || '',
    mediaType: p.mediaType || p.type || '',
    publishedAt: p.timestamp || p.createdAt || ''
}));
```

**LinkedIn normalization**:
```js
return posts.map(p => ({
    text: p.text || '',
    imageUrl: p.imageUrl || '',
    thumbnailUrl: p.thumbnailUrl || '',
    contentUrl: p.postUrl || p.url || '',
    likesCount: Number(p.likesCount || 0),
    commentsCount: Number(p.commentsCount || 0),
    sharesCount: Number(p.sharesCount || 0),
    postType: p.postType || '',
    articleTitle: p.articleTitle || '',
    articleUrl: p.articleUrl || '',
    publishedAt: p.createdAt || ''
}));
```

**Twitter normalization**:
```js
return tweets.map(t => ({
    id: String(t.id || ''),
    text: t.text || '',
    imageUrl: t.imageUrl || '',
    contentUrl: t.postUrl || t.url || '',
    likesCount: Number(t.likesCount || 0),
    sharesCount: Number(t.retweetsCount || 0),
    commentsCount: Number(t.repliesCount || 0),
    repliesCount: Number(t.repliesCount || 0),
    publishedAt: t.createdAt || ''
}));
```

**YouTube normalization**:
```js
return videos.map(v => ({
    title: v.title || '',
    imageUrl: v.thumbnailUrl || '',
    thumbnailUrl: v.thumbnailUrl || '',
    contentUrl: v.url || '',
    viewsCount: Number(v.viewCount || 0),
    likesCount: Number(v.likeCount || 0),
    commentsCount: Number(v.commentCount || 0),
    duration: v.duration || '',
    publishedAt: v.uploadedAt || v.date || ''
}));
```

**GitHub normalization**:
```js
return repos.map(r => ({
    title: r.name || '',
    description: r.description || '',
    language: r.language || '',
    stars: Number(r.stars || 0),
    forks: Number(r.forks || 0),
    contentUrl: r.url || '',
    publishedAt: r.updatedAt || ''
}));
```

